Image SXM history        v1.54        ( Apr 94 - Jun 94 )____________________________________________________________________________________v1.54    ·8    (19 Jun 94)Added features:	¥	To make Image SXM more flexible in handling STM files, the file identifier labels are now user-selectable. In earlier versions, they were preset to the Omicron settings of 'ta' and 'tp' for the image and parameter files, respectively. Image SXM still defaults to the Omicron settings, but these can now be changed in the STM Options dialog box. Filenames can have any characters prefixing these identifiers and any characters suffixing the file number providing that the additional strings of characters do not contain an embedded identifier Ð the longer they are, the more chance there is of accidentally including an additional identifier in the filename.	¥	A new 'Change File Names...' command has been added to the STM menu. This allows filenames to be changed to names that are more meaningful to the user. If an SXM file or folder has not been selected previously then a folder must be selected Ð this folder becomes the default folder for subsequent operations. The identifier labels to be found and replaced do not have to be the same length. The image and parameter file identifier labels must be different.	¥	A new 'Add Border...' command has been added to the STM menu. This places the image in the front window into the centre of a larger window, preserving all the calibration data of the original image. By selecting the default option for the size of the border, image rotation operations can be carried out without clipping the corners of the image. Larger or smaller borders (user-selectable size) can be added if desired.Bug fixes:	¥	None.Other changes:	¥	Pressing the cmd-key together with any of the arrow keys when an STM image is in the front window will attempt to load the image with the next highest (->) or lowest (<-) file number. A file error is generated if another folder has been accessed since the original image was opened. ____________________________________________________________________________________v1.54    ·7    (12 Jun 94)Added features:	¥	None. Bug fixes:	¥	Fixed a bug in the 'ReCompensate' procedure that caused a crash if the rectangle used to define the region over which the tilt compensation was to be carried out was selected using 'Select All' rather than by dragging a rectangle.Other changes:	¥	Minor changes to the positions of items in various dialog boxes to make them consistent with Apple guidelines.____________________________________________________________________________________v1.54    ·6    (9 Jun 94)Added features:	¥	None. Bug fixes:	¥	The 'Browse Images...' procedures are now a little more robust when browsing through folders that contain either no images or images of the wrong type (i.e., STM images when the procedure is expecting SEM images).Other changes:	¥	The Results window now has an extra option, referred to as 'User4' in the code and labelled 'Title' in the Results window. This records the active window title every time a measurement is made. This is useful if you want to jump from one image to another, recording measurements from more than one____________________________________________________________________________________v1.54    ·5    (8 Jun 94)Added features:	¥	None. Bug fixes:	¥	A bug was found in the original code for Image that gave incorrect tabbing in the Results window. This has been fixed.Other changes:	¥	The addition of an option to display the units used for each of the measurements in the Results window has been rewritten so that it does not use the 'User2' data structure. This means that it no longer interferes with any macros which use this structure. A new data structure has been created (referred to as 'User3' in the code and labelled 'Units' in the Results window) to hold the units for each measurement. If all this means nothing to you, then you don't have to worry about it. ____________________________________________________________________________________v1.54    ·4    (5 Jun 94)Added features:	¥	A new 'Browse Images...' command has been added to the SEM menu. The user can specify a folder to browse through and select the reduction factor to be used to display the images as a montage. If an SXM file or folder has not been selected previously then a folder must be selected Ð this folder becomes the default folder for subsequent operations. The file name is displayed in the corner of each image. Browsing can be aborted when an image is being displayed (with cmd-period). Double-clicking on an image will load that image into a separate window, providing that it is one of the first 36 images that are displayed in the most recent 'Browse SEM Images' window.	¥	A new 'Browse Images...' command has been added to the STM menu. The user can specify a folder to browse through, select a range of file numbers and the size of a window in which the images will be displayed as a montage. If an SXM file or folder has not been selected previously then a folder must be selected Ð this folder becomes the default folder for subsequent operations. The file number, image size, tip voltage and tunnelling current are displayed in the corners of each image. If the largest display window size is selected, then the window is scaled to fit the monitor and the file numbers are displayed in the centre of each image using a larger font size. Browsing can be aborted when an image is being displayed (with cmd-period). Double-clicking on an image will load that image into a separate window, providing that it is one of the first 36 images that are displayed in the most recent 'Browse STM Images' window.	¥	A new 'ReCompensate' command has been added to the STM menu. After an image has been opened and displayed, then the image can be reopened (into a separate window) with the XY tilt or Z drift compensation calculated over a user-selected rectangle drawn onto the original image. If a rectangle has not been drawn in an STM image window, then this menu item is dimmed.Bug fixes:	¥	It was found that sometimes the STM parameter file contains values for the size of the image (number of lines and number of pixels per line) that do not correspond to the actual image dimensions. To deal with such a situation, Image now calculates these numbers using the X and Y image dimensions (in ) and the X and Y step size (in ).Other changes:	¥	Holding down the shift key when closing a window bypasses the usual 'Save changes...?' dialog box if the window has been changed since it was opened or last saved. Use this with caution.	¥	The tilt compensation algorithms now look at Z values at XY positions that are inset from the edges of the images by 0, 20 or 50 pixels, depending on the image size. These inset values are overridden if the 'ReCompensate' command is used (see above).	¥	There are now three variants of the original Image application Ð Image SEM, STM and SXM. There are no functional differences between them. The differences between them are purely cosmetic Ð the appearance of the splash screen when the application is launched, etc. This has been done so that users see an acronym with which they are familiar.____________________________________________________________________________________v1.54    ·3    (1 Jun 94)Development version.  Tested by STM users in Liverpool. Not on general release.____________________________________________________________________________________v1.54    ·2    (25 May 94)Development version.  Tested by STM users in Liverpool. Not on general release.____________________________________________________________________________________v1.54    ·1    (22 May 94)Added features:	¥	Image can now handle dual STM images (i.e., two images of the same area taken with two different sample voltages or tunnelling currents). The two images are renamed to make them distinct and can be saved individually. Because they have been renamed, the 'Rescale' command does not work for dual images.  This may be rectified in a later version.	¥	Option-clicking in the Plot window of an STM image will attempt to resize the plot such that the vertical and horizontal scales are the same, thus giving an undistorted height profile. Option-clicking a second time redraws the original profile plot. If the Z variation is small, requiring a Plot window wider than the display monitor, then the plot is not drawn.Bug fixes:	¥	The 'Rescale' command now correctly recalculates the Z values after the greyscale has been changed (in version Æ3 the scale did not get inverted, so that white pixels had a lower Z value than black pixels). If the command is called more than once, then the original Z values are forgotten. Note that the Z scale is correct, but the actual values assigned to each pixel may have an arbitrary offset relative to their original values. Other changes:	¥	Due to spurious Z values along the edges of dual images, the tilt compensation algorithms now look at Z values at XY positions that are inset from the edges of the images by 10 or 20 pixels, depending on the image size.	¥	When the cursor is in a Plot window of an STM image, the X and 'Y' (i.e., Z height) values are both displayed in .	¥	Minor changes to SEM menu layout.	¥	Some SEM and STM menu items are now dimmed if the front window is not an SXM image.	¥	Maximum image size is now limited to 2048 x 2048.____________________________________________________________________________________v1.54   Æ3    (15 May 94)Released in Birmingham and Liverpool IRCs for general use.____________________________________________________________________________________v1.54    §    (AprÐMay 94)Development version. Tested by SEM users in Birmingham and STM users in Liverpool.____________________________________________________________________________________v1.54    alpha    (up to Apr 94)Development version. Not released.____________________________________________________________________________________